+# Countertop Air-Fryer Comparison
+
+Applying the final criteria leaves three finalists: width at or below 14.5 inches, capacity of at least 5 quarts, a warranty of at least one year, a dishwasher-safe basket, and controls that are not touch-only. They are ranked by lowest noise, with lower regular price reserved as the tiebreaker and with regular rather than promotional prices reported.
+
+| Rank | Model | Regular price | Width (in) | Capacity (qt) | Warranty | Controls | Noise (dBA) | Why it fits |
+|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---|
+| 1 | LumaKitchen HushFry 6 | $229 | 14.3 | 6.0 | 2 years | dial + buttons | 39 | Quietest eligible model; its dishwasher-safe basket, 6-quart capacity, two-year warranty, and non-touch-only controls meet every retained filter. |
+| 2 | Northstar CrispDial 5 | $169 | 12.8 | 5.0 | 2 years | dual dials | 42 | Shares the next-lowest noise result and wins the regular-price tiebreaker; its dishwasher-safe basket, compact width, two-year warranty, and physical dials meet every retained filter. |
+| 3 | Cedar & Coil AeroRoast 7 | $219 | 14.4 | 7.0 | 1 year | dial + buttons | 42 | Ties the runner-up on noise but loses the regular-price tiebreaker; its roomy dishwasher-safe basket, qualifying warranty, compliant width, and physical controls still fit every filter. |
+
+## Recommendation
+
+Choose the LumaKitchen HushFry 6 because its 39 dBA result makes it the quietest eligible finalist while its 6-quart basket and two-year warranty remain practical. Its tradeoff is price: at a $229 regular price, it costs $60 more than the least expensive finalist.
+
+## Runner-up
+
+The Northstar CrispDial 5 is the runner-up because its 42 dBA result ties Cedar & Coil and its $169 regular price wins the tiebreaker. Its 5-quart capacity is the smallest of the finalists and it is 3 dBA noisier than the winner, but its two-year warranty is a useful advantage.
